  "notes": [
    "Flavor Profile: Delivers a full-bodied, low-acidity cup characterized by bold, earthy, and warm spicy tasting notes with a subtle dark-cocoa sweetness.",
    "Recommended Brewing Methods: Well-suited for immersion methods like French press and cold brew, as well as espresso, which highlight heavy body and rich undertones while minimizing harshness.",
    "Brewing Ratio & Water Temperature: Use a 1:15 to 1:16 coffee-to-water ratio (about 2 tablespoons or 10–12 grams per 6 ounces of water) with water heated between 195°F and 200°F (90°C–93°C) to prevent scorching the dark roast.",
    "Grind Guidelines: Grind beans right before brewing for maximum freshness—coarse for French press or cold brew, medium for automatic drip or pour-over, and fine for espresso.",
    "Storage Advice: Keep whole beans in an airtight, opaque container in a cool, dry cupboard at room temperature; avoid the refrigerator or freezer, which introduce moisture and dull aromatic oils."
